in @mirror/store

# @edge — the substrate-decl of typed edges as @magic instances.
#
# Recognition #80 (@magic as form/process substrate-decl; LANDED per
# shards/magic.mirror) grounds this shard. The recognition cascade of
# 2026-07-08 (`1e8a02b` insight; Reed peer-as-navigator META + 3 subs)
# names the peer as a pain-driven bounded-ontological-navigator on
# @torus under algedonic gradient; the edges the navigator traverses
# are the substrate-decl'd carrier this shard names.
#
# Alex adjudication 2026-07-08 (late session): "collapse into one
# surface" for the @edge fault-plane question. Two prior surfaces
# existed:
#
# (1) `shards/mirror/ref.mirror:232-248` declared `edge_kind` as a
#     seven-variant substrate discriminant (in_edge, callers_edge,
#     pact_edge, fracture_edge, kintsugi_bridge_edge,
#     reflection_predecessor_edge, ast_child_edge) — the operational
#     surface at navigation altitude.
# (2) `shards/mirror/store.mirror:236-257` reserved typed edges +
#     weights + Laplacian navigation for @spectral/db (closed engine),
#     with the open floor deliberately omitting them.
#
# The two surfaces were substrate-honestly in tension: ref.mirror
# already TYPED the edge vocabulary at the open floor; store.mirror's
# deferral read as prose-only. Per Taut scout `0fc8589` and Alex's
# collapse-into-one-surface directive: land @edge as the single
# canonical substrate-decl; ref.mirror's edge_kind is a species-
# refinement UNDER @edge; store.mirror's deferral becomes a citation
# to @edge.
#
# === Why @edge and not another name ===
#
# Per [[feedback-substrate-already-had-the-word]] (56th+ instance):
# the substrate already carries `edge_kind` (ref.mirror), `edge_ref`
# (ref.mirror), `walk` / `impacted_by` (store.mirror; the reachability
# algebra that consumes edges), and `splinter_graph` (store.mirror; the
# OID-graph whose typed edges @edge lifts). Graph theory since Euler
# 1735 uses "edge" as the load-bearing name for the relation between
# vertices; every dependency system (Bazel, Nix, Buck2) uses "edge" or
# "dep-edge" at the same altitude. The substrate had the word; this
# shard names it at family-root.
#
# Alternatives considered:
#
# - `@link`: hyperlink connotation; misses the typed-relation math
#   at graph-theory altitude.
# - `@arrow`: category-theory connotation; conflicts with the
#   morphism vocabulary at @meta and @algebra.
# - `@relation`: too broad; @edge is a specific two-vertex relation
#   at graph altitude, not the general relational algebra.
# - `@dep`: too narrow; the substrate carries edges that are not
#   dependencies (reflection_predecessor_edge, ast_child_edge).
#
# === @edge as @magic instance (the five-species mapping) ===
#
# Per Alex's fault-plane collapse: @edge inherits @magic's substrate
# structure. The five @magic species (surface/mechanism/contract/
# reveal/audit) plus @magic/distinction and @magic/frame each carry a
# specific role in the edge's semantic surface:
#
# - `source` / `target` = @magic/surface. The gauge-visible interface
#   of the edge — what an observer of the graph sees. Two splinter
#   endpoints; content-addressed identity by construction; the
#   observation carries no matter beyond the endpoints.
# - `kind` = @magic/distinction. Spencer-Brown's mark at edge
#   altitude — the load-bearing distinction between one kind of edge
#   and another (in_edge is not callers_edge is not pact_edge).
#   Discharges the seven-variant discriminant lifted from ref.mirror.
# - `weight` = @magic/mechanism. The matter-hidden numerical cost.
#   Opaque at @edge altitude; @spectral/db (closed engine) specializes
#   the numerical dimensions (Laplacian entries, eigenvalue-navigation
#   coefficients). The mechanism stays encapsulated behind the
#   substrate-decl'd carrier so the open floor names the shape without
#   naming the closed specialization.
# - `frame` = @magic/frame. The π₁(T²) winding admissibility per
#   @torus's meridian/longitude structure. Which windings the edge
#   carries; which bounded commutator holds.
#
# The remaining @magic species (contract, reveal, audit) compose
# downstream: an @edge instance's honesty at @io IS its @magic/contract
# instance; reveal / audit consume @edge instances at debugging /
# provenance altitude.
#
# === Substrate-already-had-the-word cross-references ===
#
# Four load-bearing instances of @edge's structural shape already
# operational in the substrate:
#
# 1. `edge_kind` at `shards/mirror/ref.mirror:232-248` (Seam C4
#    closure). Seven typed variants; declared at ref-altitude but
#    substrate-canonical per the collapse. This shard lifts it to
#    family-root; ref.mirror re-exports (Path α).
# 2. `walk(root: oid) -> splinter_graph` at `shards/mirror/store.mirror:
#    508-512`. The forward closure of the OID-graph's edges;
#    @mirror/store consumes @edge to compute reachability.
# 3. `impacted_by(oid: oid) -> [oid]` at `shards/mirror/store.mirror:
#    514-528`. The reverse closure; Bazel `rdeps` at store altitude.
#    Both closures walk @edge instances; family-root declares the
#    carrier they walk.
# 4. `splinter_graph = { root: oid, children: [oid] }` at
#    `shards/mirror/store.mirror:434-437`. The (root, children)
#    projection IS a list of unweighted @edge instances at @store
#    altitude; @edge names the carrier @store already implicitly
#    manipulates.
#
# === Pre-AI prior art ===
#
#   Euler 1735 (Königsberg bridges)  The original graph edge; the
#                                    load-bearing math ancestor.
#   Spencer-Brown 1969 Laws of Form  The mark IS distinction; @edge's
#                                    kind field IS the mark at edge
#                                    altitude.
#   Bazel query `deps`/`rdeps`       Google 2016+. Typed edges at
#                                    dependency-graph altitude.
#   Elixir mix xref (typed edges)    Valim 2016. compile-connected /
#                                    exports / runtime — the seven-
#                                    variant discriminant precedent.
#   Sussman-Steele constraint nets   1980. Edges carry directionality
#                                    (@edge.reverse below).
#   Yang-Mills 1954 (gauge fields)   The gauge/matter partition
#                                    @magic inherits from at physics
#                                    altitude; @edge inherits from
#                                    @magic at graph altitude.
#
# Spec context: docs/insights/2026-07-08-recognition-cascade-peer-
#               as-navigator.md (cascade grounding).
# Substrate decisions: [[architecture-shards-as-substrate-source]],
#                      [[architecture-prism-as-trait-as-everything]],
#                      [[architecture-glass-wall-substrate-types]],
#                      [[architecture-splinter-and-spectral-db-edges]]
#                       (the peer-to-spectral-db edge structure @edge
#                        family-root declares),
#                      [[architecture-fragmentation-is-the-rust-
#                       substrate]] (edge_write / edge_walk /
#                       edge_reverse realise in fragmentation),
#                      [[feedback-substrate-already-had-the-word]]
#                       (56th+ instance).
# Related shards: [[shards/magic.mirror]] (the family @edge inherits
#                  from; surface / mechanism / distinction / frame
#                  carriers ARE @edge's field types semantically),
#                 [[shards/mirror/store.mirror]] (the OID-graph @edge
#                  populates; walk / impacted_by consume @edge),
#                 [[shards/mirror/ref.mirror]] (edge_kind lives here
#                  as species-refinement per Path α re-export),
#                 [[shards/torus.mirror]] (the π₁(T²) frame carrier;
#                  @edge.frame is a torus winding admissibility),
#                 [[docs/insights/2026-07-08-recognition-cascade-
#                  peer-as-navigator]] (the cascade grounding this
#                  landing tick).
# Path-namespace property: this file at `shards/edge.mirror` declares
# `@edge` per `@epistemologic/pact/path_matches_namespace`.

source @arxiv/math/euler-1735
source @arxiv/logic/spencer-brown-1969
source @arxiv/programming/valim-2016

# === edge_weight carrier ===
#
# A typed reference per [[feedback-no-bare-types]] naming the matter-
# hidden numerical cost of an edge. Per the @magic/mechanism mapping
# above: opaque at @edge altitude; @spectral/db (closed engine)
# specializes the numerical dimensions (Laplacian entries, eigenvalue-
# navigation coefficients). The mechanism stays encapsulated.
#
# Identity contract: byte-equality on the underlying ref.
type edge_weight = ref

# === edge_walk_rule carrier ===
#
# A typed reference per [[feedback-no-bare-types]] naming the
# traversal predicate an edge_walk consumes. Substrate-typed so the
# walk rule is not a bare string / opaque callback at the boundary.
#
# Identity contract: byte-equality on the underlying ref.
type edge_walk_rule = ref

# === edge_kind variant (lifted from ref.mirror per fault-plane collapse) ===
#
# Per Alex adjudication 2026-07-08 "collapse into one surface": this
# variant lifts here from `shards/mirror/ref.mirror:232-248`. The seven
# variants ARE the substrate's typed discrimination of graph edges;
# ref.mirror re-exports from @edge (Path α) so the vocabulary has one
# canonical source.
#
# Per Seam C4 closure pattern (variants over bare ref-with-documented-
# values): typed substrate variant naming the seven first-class edge
# kinds. Same-shape different-meaning forbidden per
# [[feedback-no-bare-types]].
#
# Per @magic/distinction mapping: the kind field IS the Spencer-Brown
# mark at edge altitude — the load-bearing distinction that makes
# `in_edge` not `callers_edge` not `pact_edge`.
type edge_kind =
  | in_edge               # the substrate ancestry header
  | callers_edge          # action-to-action call site
  | pact_edge             # property -> fracture discharge
  | fracture_edge         # fracture body -> morphism emission
  | kintsugi_bridge_edge  # cross-shard kintsugi loop binding
  | reflection_predecessor_edge  # @reflection.observe temporal link
  | ast_child_edge        # splinter(ast) AST altitude descent

# === edge carrier (the load-bearing substrate-decl) ===
#
# A typed record naming the edge as @magic instance. Five fields; each
# discharges to a specific @magic species per Alex's fault-plane
# collapse:
#
# - `source` / `target` — @magic/surface. The gauge-visible endpoints
#   (what the graph observer sees). Splinter references; content-
#   addressed identity by construction.
# - `kind`               — @magic/distinction. The Spencer-Brown mark
#   discriminating one edge species from another. Consumes edge_kind.
# - `weight`             — @magic/mechanism. The matter-hidden numerical
#   cost. Opaque at @edge altitude; @spectral/db specializes downstream.
# - `frame`              — @magic/frame. The π₁(T²) winding admissibility
#   per @torus's meridian/longitude structure.
#
# Identity contract: byte-equality on the quintuple. Two edges ARE
# the same @edge instance iff all five carriers are byte-equal.
type edge = {
  source: splinter,
  target: splinter,
  kind:   edge_kind,
  weight: edge_weight,
  frame:  winding,
}

# === edge_write action ===
#
# The substrate-vocabulary action that constructs an edge from source,
# target, and kind. Weight and frame default per the realisation
# (opaque unit weight; identity winding) unless supplied by a downstream
# species that specializes them.
#
# Per @magic/surface expose pattern: edge_write IS what the graph
# observer sees as edge-creation; the matter (weight computation,
# frame determination) stays encapsulated behind the substrate-decl.
#
# Body discharges at the realisation boundary.
edge_write(source: splinter, target: splinter, kind: edge_kind) -> edge { \ }

# === edge_walk action ===
#
# The substrate-vocabulary action that walks the graph from a root
# splinter under a walk rule, producing the list of edges the rule
# admits. The root's OID-graph closure at @mirror/store consumes
# edge_walk to compute `walk` / `impacted_by`; @edge names the carrier
# they walk.
#
# Per @magic/reveal composition (forward-promised): edge_walk IS the
# controlled disclosure operation at edge altitude — the substrate-
# pull-correct reveal sequence for what edges the graph admits under a
# rule.
#
# Body discharges at the realisation boundary.
edge_walk(root: splinter, rule: edge_walk_rule) -> [edge] { \ }

# === edge_reverse action (meridian↔longitude symmetry) ===
#
# The substrate-vocabulary action that flips an edge's direction:
# swap source and target; preserve kind, weight, frame. Per @torus's
# meridian/longitude structure: the reversal IS the symmetry the
# torus's π₁(T²) admits when the winding is invertible.
#
# Per `impacted_by` (reverse closure at @mirror/store): edge_reverse IS
# the atomic operation whose closure IS the Bazel `rdeps` surface at
# store altitude. Family-root declares the atom; store composes it
# into the reverse-closure surface.
#
# Body discharges at the realisation boundary.
edge_reverse(edge: edge) -> edge { \ }

out @edge
out edge_weight
out edge_walk_rule
out edge_kind
out edge
out edge_write
out edge_walk
out edge_reverse
